 "about": "The registered taking rules of TIME-AS-FOLD-20261125-001A with their cost: FD 3.3's vector and one component added here, kinds of birth treated differently (1 = every birth treated alike, 2 = joins against offshoots, 3 = offshoots also treated differently by the kind of their parent: of joins, of offshoots). The number of the parent's parents lies within the first parent step, which STEPS-k already looks at, so the rules by the kind of the parent add only that component. Equivalences, by construction: STEPS-k for offshoots of start knots takes nothing (a start knot has no ancestor), so the STEPS family by the kind of the parent has three members for each k (offshoots of joins; of offshoots; both, which is STEPS-k); MET with neither clause is the control.",
